fillReadT -- a reader for fill= (SEQ 547 recon, SEQ 549 rulings). displayFillRT takes the field's own fill first, then its style's fillColor. A value starting with # is parsed where it sits, on both. Any other plain value is looked up by name at draw, and a miss refuses by name. fill is not inherited: the reader reads the field's own attribute and never walks to a parent.

Every spelling runs on fill and on fillColor, side by side. The move rows are the point of := against =: after a write to the source, the held draw changes and the copy does not.

Pinned on trunk, born red, before the build. No form is respelled (SEQ 549 R3), so this fixture is the only user of the reader; fill=off and bare fill refuse by name.
